(D4 — Discrepancy 4 repro: LANGUAGE.md:4306-4308 says
 examples/supervisor.vox "is this loop as a runnable program". It is not
 the same program. The manual's snippet opens with
 `see process version "0.1" from "./libprocess.lib".` and calls `crashed`
 and `'exited normally'` from that library; the example file carries its
 own comment "Deliberately no `see`: `the reaped status` is a complete
 compiler feature, and this test must pass with nothing installed at all",
 defines its own decoders, and prints six lines about two jobs rather than
 the snippet's one.
 This repro is the manual's snippet with its `see` line removed — which is
 what "the example is this loop" would have to mean, since the example has
 no `see` line — and it does not compile.
 Ran, from the repo root:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm \
   /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox \
   docs/ledger/probes/process-control/D4.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   error: Unknown function: crashed
   error: Unknown function: signal of
   error: Unknown function: exited normally
   (no binary produced; compile error)
)

Set pid to fork the process.
If pid is 0 then,
    Exit 0.

a timer called clock.
Start the clock.
a boolean called 'child is still running' is true.
a boolean called 'child was killed' is false.
While 'child is still running',
    Set 'reap result' to reap child pid without waiting,
    If 'reap result' is pid then,
        Set 'child is still running' to false.
    If 'child is still running' then,
        a number called 'milliseconds waited' is the clock's elapsed in milliseconds,
        If 'milliseconds waited' is greater than 5000 then,
            Send signal 9 to process pid,
            Set 'reap result' to reap child pid,
            Set 'child is still running' to false,
            Set 'child was killed' to true.
    If 'child is still running' then,
        Wait 10 milliseconds.

If 'child was killed' then,
    Print "hang".
If 'child was killed' is false then,
    Set status to the reaped status,
    If crashed of status then,
        Print "died by signal {'signal of' of status}".
    If 'exited normally' of status then,
        Print "exit {'exit code of' of status}".
